    {
      "source": "Doctors of Running",
      "priority": 3,
      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2025/12/mizuno-wave-sky-9-review-2025.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The high-stack setup (44/38 mm) is protective but rides moderately cushioned and firm-leaning after break-in, with a less clean heel feel/transition.",
        "Responsiveness: Bounce and energy return are limited at easy paces and improve mainly when the midsole is loaded hard; overall feel is not especially snappy.",
        "Stability: The shoe is very stiff with minimal flex, and its wide base/flare adds lateral stability after break-in, but a loose heel fit can reduce rearfoot security.",
        "Durability: Durability is a standout, with a tough X10 outsole, plentiful rubber, strong wet-road grip, and an overall tank-like build expected to last."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Road Trail Run",
      "priority": 4,
      "url": "https://www.roadtrailrun.com/2025/07/mizuno-wave-sky-9-review-6-comparisons.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: True max-cushion build (44 mm heel/38 mm forefoot) with soft Enerzy NXT over denser EVA delivers deep impact protection, friendly heel landings, and forgiving but controlled forefoot feel.",
        "Responsiveness: Supercritical foam provides noticeable energy return and bounce, with more forefoot rebound at moderate paces; the ride is responsive for a max trainer but not highly snappy/aggressive.",
        "Stability: Broad platform, Wave-shaped lower EVA, stout heel counter, and secure upper create strong torsional/lateral control, straight tracking, and smooth stable transitions.",
        "Durability: Deep segmented outsole rubber plus reinforced key wear zones indicate strong outsole wear resistance and long-lasting ride consistency over high mileage."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Believe in the Run",
      "priority": 5,
      "url": "https://believeintherun.com/shoe-reviews/mizuno-wave-sky-9-review/",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: 44/38 mm stack with Enerzy NXT feels super-soft and pillowy, giving soft heel landings, strong impact protection, and a smooth heel-to-forefoot transition.",
        "Responsiveness: Enerzy NXT delivers noticeable bounce/energy return (especially for midfoot striking) and feels lively for easy miles, but the shoe is too bulky to feel snappy at faster paces.",
        "Stability: Multi-density Foam Wave plus the firmer lower Enerzy layer keeps the ride stable despite high softness; reviewers noted a sturdy heel counter, secure lockdown, and minimal heel slip/lateral movement.",
        "Durability: The X10 carbon rubber outsole is described as durable with good wet traction, and after roughly 30 miles reviewers reported no significant outsole wear."
      ]
    }
